# Threshold evaluator (issue #22) - runs once a minute against Metrion's own
# database. See organizational/agent-deployment-runbook.md for the systemd
# unit/timer and the env-file transfer convention (scp under `umask 077`,
# installed at mode 600, owner `deploy`).

# Reused as-is by @metrion/db's createPool() - same variable the migration
# runner and every other Metrion service already read. Not set here on
# purpose in dev: the local-dev default (docker-compose.dev.yml's `db`
# service) already matches createPool()'s own fallback.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://metrion:metrion@localhost:5432/metrion

# Plain SMTP via nodemailer - every candidate email provider speaks SMTP, so
# changing provider is an env-file edit, not a code change. Provider is
# tentatively Brevo's free tier (~300 emails/day, EEA processor) - NOT YET
# CREATED. This account can only be created by the account owner; see
# organizational/agent-deployment-runbook.md's "Threshold evaluator" section
# for the remaining pre-flight steps.
SMTP_HOST=smtp-relay.brevo.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=<brevo-smtp-login>
# Never committed, never logged - see src/mailer.ts's doc comment.
SMTP_PASSWORD=<brevo-smtp-key>
ALERT_FROM=alerts@<domain>

# Quota/flapping guards - see src/mailer.ts. EVALUATOR_DAILY_EMAIL_CAP left
# unset on purpose: src/config/index.ts's own default is 75, raised from the
# original 50 after that cap silently dropped notifications on 2026-10-01
# during an unrelated flapping-metric incident. Set a real number here only
# if a project needs a different per-day ceiling.
# EVALUATOR_DAILY_EMAIL_CAP=75
EVALUATOR_COOLDOWN_MINUTES=60

# status_events retention - see src/evaluate.ts's pruneOldStatusEvents.
EVALUATOR_STATUS_EVENT_RETENTION_DAYS=180

# Skips real SMTP entirely (nodemailer's own JSON transport, logged to
# stdout instead) - the one way to run a real cycle against a real database
# with no real SMTP credentials at all. Never set on the server unit once
# real credentials are wired.
EVALUATOR_DRY_RUN=false
